From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] accel/rocket: retire an RK3576 pooling job on the PPU's
 completion

0012 retires a job when the DPU raises its own completion in
INTERRUPT_RAW_STATUS, because PC_DONE means the program counter finished
issuing the task and not that the write DMA has drained.  That is the
right signal for a convolution or a matmul, and there is one class of
program for which it can never arrive: a POOL.

PC_OPERATION_ENABLE is a per-block bitmap.  A convolution enables
CNA/CORE/DPU/DPU_RDMA with 0x1d; a pool enables PPU and PPU_RDMA with
0x60, and the two bit sets are disjoint.  A pooling program has no DPU
stage at all, so DPU_0/DPU_1 never set for it and every pooling job
retires on the dpu_grace_us deadline instead -- paid in full, on every
submit.

Measured through the userspace pooling entry on an H96 MAX M9, the wait
for the output BO on a 1024x7x7 k7 average pool [HW sweep]:

  dpu_grace_us     500     250     100
  wait (us)        641     389     213

-- it tracks the grace period count for count, which is what says the
job is not retiring on a completion at all.  On MobileNetV1-224 that is
640 us of the pooling layer's 1.48 ms and 640 us of the whole 6.2 ms
inference.

The PPU raises its own completion in the same register, two bits over.
Wait for that instead when the job's last program is a PPU program.
Which class a job is in is not visible to the driver at PC_DONE time and
is entirely visible to userspace, which wrote PC_OPERATION_ENABLE -- so
it is a per-job flag, the same shape 0017 uses for the other class that
cannot be told apart from the inside.

DRM_ROCKET_JOB_PPU_DONE selects the PPU bits in place of the DPU ones,
latched per submit into the core so the poll callback still needs no job
pointer.  Setting it on a job whose last program is a convolution costs
that job the grace period and nothing else.  A job that MIXES DPU and
PPU programs in one chained stream must not set it, because an interior
program's PPU bit would retire the job while a later DPU write was still
draining; the flag is documented as naming the LAST program's class.

The interface version goes to 1.3 so userspace can tell a kernel that
honors the flag from one that ignores it -- ignoring it is the old
behavior, which is correct and slower.

RK3588 takes a completion interrupt and does not poll, so it is
untouched.

Signed-off-by: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_core.h |  6 ++++++
 drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_drv.c  |  3 ++-
 drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_job.c  | 33 ++++++++++++++++++++++--------
 drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_job.h  |  9 ++++++++
 include/uapi/drm/rocket_accel.h    | 20 ++++++++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 61 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_core.h b/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_core.h
index 5c2df4fdf..3811bb562 100644
--- a/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_core.h
+++ b/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_core.h
@@ -95,6 +95,12 @@ struct rocket_core {
 	 * DRM_ROCKET_JOB_NO_DPU_DONE) so the poll timer needs no job pointer.
 	 */
 	unsigned int poll_grace_us;
+	/*
+	 * Which INTERRUPT_RAW_STATUS bits are this job's completion.  The DPU's
+	 * for a convolution or a matmul, the PPU's for a pooling program, which
+	 * has no DPU stage at all.  Latched per submit for the same reason.
+	 */
+	u32 poll_done_mask;
 
 	struct drm_gpu_scheduler sched;
 	u64 fence_context;
diff --git a/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_drv.c b/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_drv.c
index 39eeef833..8f1be538b 100644
--- a/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_drv.c
@@ -164,6 +164,7 @@ DEFINE_DRM_ACCEL_FOPS(rocket_accel_driver_fops);
  *         is refused with -E2BIG rather than silently ignored.
  * - 1.1 - adds DRM_ROCKET_JOB_BATCHED (per-job chained submit).
  * - 1.2 - adds DRM_ROCKET_JOB_NO_DPU_DONE (per-job completion-class hint).
+ * - 1.3 - adds DRM_ROCKET_JOB_PPU_DONE (retire on the PPU's completion).
  *
  * Userspace MUST NOT self-chain a job's regcmd layout unless the driver reports
  * >= 1.1: an older kernel does not know the flag, would run that chained layout
@@ -171,7 +172,7 @@ DEFINE_DRM_ACCEL_FOPS(rocket_accel_driver_fops);
  */
 static const struct drm_driver rocket_drm_driver = {
 	.major			= 1,
-	.minor			= 2,
+	.minor			= 3,
 	.driver_features	= DRIVER_COMPUTE_ACCEL | DRIVER_GEM,
 	.open			= rocket_open,
 	.postclose		= rocket_postclose,
diff --git a/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_job.c b/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_job.c
index da4f4241b..3139f09a3 100644
--- a/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_job.c
+++ b/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_job.c
@@ -314,6 +314,11 @@ static void rocket_job_hw_submit(struct rocket_core *core, struct rocket_job *jo
 		core->poll_grace_us = job->no_dpu_done
 			? READ_ONCE(rocket_dpu_blind_us)
 			: READ_ONCE(rocket_dpu_grace_us);
+		core->poll_done_mask = job->ppu_done
+			? (PC_INTERRUPT_RAW_STATUS_PPU_0 |
+			   PC_INTERRUPT_RAW_STATUS_PPU_1)
+			: (PC_INTERRUPT_RAW_STATUS_DPU_0 |
+			   PC_INTERRUPT_RAW_STATUS_DPU_1);
 		atomic_set(&core->poll_active, 1);
 		hrtimer_start(&core->poll_timer, rocket_poll_period(),
 			      HRTIMER_MODE_REL);
@@ -587,17 +592,19 @@ static enum hrtimer_restart rocket_poll_timer_fn(struct hrtimer *timer)
 		    PC_INTERRUPT_MASK_RK3576_PC_DONE_1))) {
 		/*
 		 * PC_DONE says the program counter finished issuing the task, not
-		 * that the DPU's write DMA has drained.  The DPU raises its own
-		 * completion -- the bit RK3588 takes as its interrupt -- tens of
-		 * microseconds later, and a fence signalled on PC_DONE hands the
-		 * caller a surface whose tail has not landed yet.  Wait for it.
+		 * that the writing block's DMA has drained.  That block raises its
+		 * own completion -- the bit RK3588 takes as its interrupt -- tens
+		 * of microseconds later, and a fence signalled on PC_DONE hands
+		 * the caller a surface whose tail has not landed yet.  Wait for
+		 * it.  WHICH block writes is the job's class: the DPU for a
+		 * convolution or a matmul, the PPU for a pooling program, which
+		 * enables no DPU stage at all.
 		 *
-		 * Bounded, so a task that raises no DPU completion at all cannot
-		 * stall behind one: after dpu_grace_us the job retires on PC_DONE
+		 * Bounded, so a task that raises no completion at all cannot
+		 * stall behind one: after the grace the job retires on PC_DONE
 		 * as it did before.
 		 */
-		if (raw & (PC_INTERRUPT_RAW_STATUS_DPU_0 |
-			   PC_INTERRUPT_RAW_STATUS_DPU_1))
+		if (raw & core->poll_done_mask)
 			goto complete;
 		if (!core->poll_pc_done_at)
 			core->poll_pc_done_at = ktime_get();
@@ -915,7 +922,8 @@ static int rocket_ioctl_submit_job(struct drm_device *dev, struct drm_file *file
 		return -EINVAL;
 
 	/* Reject unknown flag bits so a future flag cannot be silently ignored. */
-	if (job->flags & ~(DRM_ROCKET_JOB_BATCHED | DRM_ROCKET_JOB_NO_DPU_DONE)) {
+	if (job->flags & ~(DRM_ROCKET_JOB_BATCHED | DRM_ROCKET_JOB_NO_DPU_DONE |
+			   DRM_ROCKET_JOB_PPU_DONE)) {
 		drm_dbg(dev, "Unknown bits set in drm_rocket_job.flags (0x%x).\n",
 			job->flags);
 		return -EINVAL;
@@ -949,6 +957,13 @@ static int rocket_ioctl_submit_job(struct drm_device *dev, struct drm_file *file
 	 */
 	rjob->no_dpu_done = !!(job->flags & DRM_ROCKET_JOB_NO_DPU_DONE);
 
+	/*
+	 * And which block's completion this job's last program raises.  A pool
+	 * is 23 PPU writes and 8 PPU_RDMA with no DPU stage, so the DPU bits
+	 * never set for it and the default wait is the grace period in full.
+	 */
+	rjob->ppu_done = !!(job->flags & DRM_ROCKET_JOB_PPU_DONE);
+
 	/*
 	 * Take the IOMMU domain reference here, while the job is still empty.
 	 * rocket_job_cleanup() puts it unconditionally, and every rejection
diff --git a/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_job.h b/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_job.h
index 148751f36..e20fa9719 100644
--- a/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_job.h
+++ b/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_job.h
@@ -54,6 +54,15 @@ struct rocket_job {
 	 */
 	bool no_dpu_done;
 
+	/*
+	 * ppu_done: userspace set DRM_ROCKET_JOB_PPU_DONE -- this job's last
+	 * program is a PPU program, whose completion is the PPU's own bit and
+	 * not the DPU's.  Selects which INTERRUPT_RAW_STATUS bits the poll
+	 * retires on.  A wrong hint costs the grace period, not correctness,
+	 * unless the job MIXES DPU and PPU programs; see the uapi flag.
+	 */
+	bool ppu_done;
+
 	/* Fence to be signaled by drm-sched once its done with the job */
 	struct dma_fence *inference_done_fence;
 
diff --git a/include/uapi/drm/rocket_accel.h b/include/uapi/drm/rocket_accel.h
index 844a3dbaf..41c3b4ab9 100644
--- a/include/uapi/drm/rocket_accel.h
+++ b/include/uapi/drm/rocket_accel.h
@@ -54,6 +54,26 @@ extern "C" {
  */
 #define DRM_ROCKET_JOB_NO_DPU_DONE	(1 << 1)
 
+/*
+ * DRM_ROCKET_JOB_PPU_DONE: this job's last program is a PPU program (pooling),
+ * whose completion is the PPU's own bit in INTERRUPT_RAW_STATUS and not the
+ * DPU's.  A PPU program enables no DPU stage at all -- PC_OPERATION_ENABLE is
+ * a per-block bitmap and a pool sets 0x60 against a convolution's 0x1d -- so
+ * the DPU bits the driver waits on by default can never set, and without this
+ * every pooling job pays @dpu_grace_us in full.
+ *
+ * Userspace knows the class because it wrote PC_OPERATION_ENABLE.  Setting it
+ * on a job whose last program is a convolution costs that job the grace period
+ * (the PPU bit never sets) and nothing else.
+ *
+ * A job that ends in a PPU program but also contains DPU programs earlier in a
+ * chained stream must NOT set this: the PPU bit an interior program raised
+ * would retire the job while a later DPU write was still draining.
+ *
+ * Only honored by a driver advertising interface version >= 1.3.
+ */
+#define DRM_ROCKET_JOB_PPU_DONE		(1 << 2)
+
 /**
  * struct drm_rocket_create_bo - ioctl argument for creating Rocket BOs.
  *
-- 
2.43.0

